Chapter: Cdx2053Range

 Pins the CDX2053 informative-proof survivor. `list-length xs` has a
 proven range of 0..4294967295 -- a real interval, with a plain Integer
 type that does not fit the field -- so storing it into a 0..4294967295
 field reaches the prover and still reports NarrowingProven (bounds
 check elided). A single-point constant proof (the-code folds to
 9002..9002) is elided silently and must NOT appear. This guards
 against over-suppression.

Section: Body

  the-code : Integer = 9002

  Wrap = record {
   code : Integer between 0 and 65535,
   big : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  from-const : Wrap
  from-const = Wrap { code = the-code, big = 0 }

  from-range : List Integer -> Wrap
  from-range (xs) = Wrap { code = 0, big = list-length xs }

  opening : Integer = (from-range [1, 2, 3]).big + from-const.code
